PROMPT 0: Foundation and contracts
You are a senior TypeScript architect. We are building SafeCircle, a scam
shield for senior citizens in India (English + Malayalam). We are building it
in layers, with one prompt per layer. This prompt creates ONLY the foundation:
project scaffold, shared contracts and documentation. Do NOT build UI screens,
the detection logic, or backend features yet.

## Tasks

1. Initialise a monorepo-style project (npm workspaces):
   - packages/engine   -> pure TypeScript scam detection engine (no React,
                          no DOM, no Node-only APIs; must run in browser,
                          Node, and later an embedded JS runtime)
   - apps/web          -> React + Vite + TypeScript (strict) + Tailwind PWA
                          (empty shell with a single placeholder page only)
   - supabase/         -> migrations folder (empty for now)
   - android/          -> placeholder README only
   - docs/
   Use TypeScript strict mode everywhere. Add ESLint, Prettier, Vitest.
   Add npm scripts: dev, build, test, lint, typecheck at the root.

2. Create shared contracts in packages/engine/src/types.ts. These are the
   contracts every later layer must follow:
   - Verdict = "SAFE" | "BE_CAREFUL" | "DANGEROUS"
   - Language = "en" | "ml"
   - SignalId (string union): AUTHORITY_CLAIM, URGENCY_THREAT, SECRECY,
     MONEY_REQUEST, SENSITIVE_INFO_REQUEST, REMOTE_ACCESS, SUSPICIOUS_URL,
     APK_INSTALL, EMERGENCY_RELATIVE, PRIZE_LOTTERY, INVESTMENT_FRAUD,
     LEGIT_CONTEXT (negative signal)
   - Indicator { signalId, weight, matchedRuleId, evidenceType } 
     NOTE: indicators must NOT contain the raw matched text, only rule ids.
   - ScanInput { text: string; source: "manual"|"share"|"notification"|
     "call_sim"; language?: Language }
   - ScanResult { score: number (0-100); verdict: Verdict; indicators:
     Indicator[]; overridesTriggered: string[]; explanation: { en: string;
     ml: string }; recommendedAction: { en: string; ml: string };
     detectionMethod: "LOCAL_RULES"|"LOCAL_AI"|"CLOUD_AI"|"HYBRID";
     rulePackVersion: string; scannedAt: string }
   - Incident (what may be stored/synced): id, scannedAt, score, verdict,
     category, signalIds[], detectionMethod, reviewed, falsePositive,
     userOutcome ("avoided"|"interacted"|"unsure"|null). NO message text.
   - GuardianAlert { id, elderId, incidentId, verdict, signalIds[],
     suggestedAction, createdAt, status }
   Export everything from the package index.

3. Define the rule-pack JSON schema (packages/engine/src/rulepack.schema.json
   plus a TS type and a runtime validator using zod):
   - version, updatedAt
   - signals: list of { signalId, weight, rules[] }
   - rules: { id, type: "regex"|"phrase"|"domain", pattern, languages[],
     notes }
   - overrides: list of { id, requires: SignalId[] (all), anyOf?: SignalId[],
     forceVerdict, minScore, reason }
   - thresholds: { carefulMin, dangerousMin }
   - templates: explanation/action text keyed by signal or override id, each
     with en and ml
   The pack is DATA, so a Kotlin interpreter can run the same pack later.

4. Create docs/ARCHITECTURE.md containing:
