## 1. Pipeline
scan(input: ScanInput, pack: RulePack): ScanResult
Steps:
a) Normalise text (see section 2).
b) Evaluate every rule in the pack and collect matched signals (de-duplicate
   per signal: a signal counts once even if several rules match it).
c) Apply LEGIT_CONTEXT as a negative signal (see section 4).
d) Compute the additive score, capped at 100 and floored at 0.
e) Apply override rules from the pack (they can only RAISE the verdict/score
   to a minimum, never lower it).
f) Map the score to a verdict using the pack thresholds (default 0-29 SAFE,
   30-59 BE_CAREFUL, 60-100 DANGEROUS).
g) Build explanation and recommendedAction in BOTH English and Malayalam from
   the pack templates. Explanations must name the detected tactics in plain
   language a senior can follow. No LLM is used in this layer.
h) Never return or log the raw message text. Indicators carry rule ids only.
The engine must be a pure function: no network, no storage, no global state,
deterministic output.

## 2. Normalisation
- Unicode NFKC, lowercase for Latin text, collapse whitespace.
- Remove zero-width characters and normalise Malayalam chillu/ZWJ/ZWNJ
  variants so that visually identical Malayalam strings match.
- Map common homoglyphs and digit/letter swaps (0/o, 1/l/i, @/a, $/s) only
  inside tokens that look like obfuscation.
- Collapse spaced-out words ("O T P", "K Y C", "a n y d e s k").
- Handle Devanagari digits and Malayalam digits in amounts and phone numbers.
- Extract URLs and domains into a separate list for the URL rules.

## 3. Rule pack content (packages/engine/rulepacks/in-v1.json)
Write a real, versioned rule pack covering English, Malayalam script AND
Manglish (Malayalam written in Latin script, e.g. "ningalude account block
aayi"), plus common Hinglish. Signals:
- AUTHORITY_CLAIM: police, CBI, ED, RBI, TRAI, income tax, customs, court,
  cyber cell, bank officer, courier/FedEx/DHL, KSEB, RTO.
- URGENCY_THREAT: arrest, warrant, blocked, suspended, legal action, expires
  today, last warning, SIM will be disconnected.
- SECRECY: do not tell anyone, do not inform family, do not disconnect the
  call, keep confidential.
- MONEY_REQUEST: transfer, pay fee/fine/deposit, refund fee, send via UPI,
  scan this QR to receive money, collect request.
- SENSITIVE_INFO_REQUEST: must detect REQUESTING info (share/send/tell/enter
  your OTP, PIN, CVV, Aadhaar, password, card number). A message that only
  DELIVERS an OTP ("Your OTP is 123456") must NOT trigger this.
- REMOTE_ACCESS: AnyDesk, TeamViewer, QuickSupport, RustDesk, screen share,
  "install this app to verify".
- SUSPICIOUS_URL: shorteners (bit.ly, tinyurl, etc. as a weak signal),
  typosquatted bank/government domains, IP-address links, suspicious TLDs,
  non-https payment links, lookalike domains (e.g. sbi-kyc-update.xyz).
  Include a small local list of official domains per bank/government body
  to compare against.
- APK_INSTALL: ".apk", "install this file", "download the app from this link"
  such as fake RTO challan, PM Kisan or bank reward APKs.
- EMERGENCY_RELATIVE: "I am your son/grandson and in trouble, send money,
  don't tell dad".
- PRIZE_LOTTERY, INVESTMENT_FRAUD (guaranteed returns, crypto/trading group,
  task/like-and-earn jobs).
- LEGIT_CONTEXT (negative weight): "never share your OTP with anyone",
  standard bank alert formats (debit/credit alert, OTP delivery), official
  sender style patterns, official domains.
Weights: start with the proposal below, capped at 100 total:
 AUTHORITY 15, URGENCY 15, SECRECY 20, MONEY 20, SENSITIVE_INFO 25,
 REMOTE_ACCESS 25, SUSPICIOUS_URL 20, APK_INSTALL 25, EMERGENCY_RELATIVE 20,
 PRIZE 15, INVESTMENT 20, LEGIT_CONTEXT -20.
Overrides (in the pack, not hardcoded):
 - REMOTE_ACCESS + any of (MONEY_REQUEST, SENSITIVE_INFO_REQUEST,
   AUTHORITY_CLAIM) -> DANGEROUS, minScore 80
 - AUTHORITY_CLAIM + (SECRECY or MONEY_REQUEST) + (URGENCY_THREAT) ->
   DANGEROUS, minScore 75
 - SECRECY + MONEY_REQUEST -> at least BE_CAREFUL, minScore 45
 - APK_INSTALL + (AUTHORITY_CLAIM or URGENCY_THREAT or MONEY_REQUEST) ->
   DANGEROUS, minScore 70
 - EMERGENCY_RELATIVE + (MONEY_REQUEST or SECRECY) -> DANGEROUS, minScore 65
 - SENSITIVE_INFO_REQUEST + (URGENCY_THREAT or AUTHORITY_CLAIM) ->
   DANGEROUS, minScore 65
 - LEGIT_CONTEXT must NOT cancel an override if SECRECY or REMOTE_ACCESS is
   present.
A single signal alone must never produce DANGEROUS unless the pack says so
explicitly.
Write templates in English and Malayalam for every signal and override. Mark
all Malayalam templates with a "needsNativeReview": true flag in the pack,
because a native speaker must review them before release.

## 4. Test suite (Vitest)
Create a dataset under packages/engine/tests/data/ as JSON files with fields
{ id, text, expectedVerdict, expectedSignals, category, language, split }.
split is "tune" or "heldout". Roughly 70% tune, 30% heldout. Heldout cases
must NOT be used while tuning weights or rules.
Minimum counts (write realistic, varied examples, not near-duplicates):
- 20 digital arrest scams, 20 fake KYC, 20 OTP phishing, 20 UPI scams
- 20 legitimate bank messages (include OTP delivery, debit/credit alerts,
  "never share your OTP" warnings, real KYC reminders from official
  domains)
- 20 legitimate government/utility notifications
- 20 Malayalam scam, 20 Malayalam legitimate
- 20 Manglish scam, 20 Manglish legitimate
- 15 APK scams, 15 emergency-relative scams, 10 investment/task scams
- 30 adversarial cases: spaced letters, homoglyphs, mixed language, zero-width
  characters, shortened URLs, emojis, all caps
- 20 hard negatives: legitimate messages that contain scary words (arrest in a
  news forward, "urgent" from a real pharmacy, "police verification" for a
  real rental, a family member genuinely asking about money without secrecy)
Tests to write:
- Per-dataset runner reporting for tune and heldout separately: confusion
  matrix by verdict, recall on DANGEROUS, false-positive rate on legitimate
  messages, and the list of misclassified ids. Print these in the console.
- Unit tests for the normaliser, each signal, each override, score capping,
  and the rule that overrides never lower a verdict.
- Privacy test: ScanResult serialised to JSON must not contain any substring
  of the input longer than 3 words.
- Determinism test: the same input gives byte-identical output.
- Performance test: a scan of a 2,000-character message completes in under
  50 ms on average.
- Conformance file: generate tests/conformance/vectors.json (input text,
  expected verdict, expected sorted signalIds, expected minimum score) from
  the heldout and unit cases. This file will be reused later by the Kotlin
  engine, so keep it free of TS-specific details.

## 5. Quality rules
- Report real metrics from the test run. Do NOT claim an accuracy percentage
  that you did not measure. Include a docs/ENGINE_REPORT.md with the measured
