## 0. Non-negotiable principles
- The app must keep working fully WITHOUT an account (local-only mode from
  Layer 2). Signing in is optional and only unlocks family features.
- Never store message text. Backend tables hold only the minimum fields in the
  Incident and GuardianAlert contracts.
- Roles are per CONNECTION, not per account. One person can be an elder in one
  connection and a guardian in another.
- The elder is always in control of who is connected and what is shared.
- Service-role keys exist only in server-side functions. Never in client
  code, never in VITE_ variables.
- If Supabase env vars are missing, the app shows a clear "family features need
  configuration" state and still works locally. No crashes.

## 1. Database (supabase/migrations/, plain SQL, numbered, idempotent)
Create these tables, all with RLS ENABLED and no policy that allows
anonymous access:
- profiles (id = auth.users.id, display_name, phone (optional), language,
  created_at)
- user_preferences (user_id, language, theme, font_scale, accent,
  reduced_motion)
- family_connections (id, elder_id, guardian_id, status: pending | active |
  revoked, created_at, approved_at, revoked_at, revoked_by,
  share_level: "none" | "alerts_only" | "alerts_and_summary",
  guardian_label)
- family_invitations (id, elder_id, token_hash (never store the raw token),
  expires_at, used_at, used_by, attempts, created_at)
- scam_incidents (id, elder_id, scanned_at, score, verdict, category,
  detection_method, reviewed, false_positive, user_outcome, rule_pack_version;
  NO message text, NO url, NO sender)
- scam_indicators (id, incident_id, signal_id)
- guardian_alerts (id, incident_id, elder_id, guardian_id, status: pending |
  delivered | seen | reviewed, created_at, seen_at, reviewed_at)
- notification_preferences (guardian_id, elder_id, channel flags: in_app,
  email, telegram, push; quiet hours optional)
- device_settings (user_id, platform, settings jsonb limited to non-sensitive
  keys)
- subscription_plans (id, code: "free" | "family", features jsonb)
- user_subscriptions (user_id, plan_id, status, period_end)
- connection_audit_log (id, connection_id or elder_id, actor_id, action:
  invited | redeemed | approved | revoked | share_level_changed |
  invite_failed, created_at). Elders can read the log for their own account.
Add sensible indexes and CHECK constraints (score 0-100, valid verdicts, valid
