## 3. Edge Functions (supabase/functions/, TypeScript/Deno)
Each validates input with zod, checks the JWT, returns generic errors, never
logs tokens or personal data.
- create-invitation: elder only. Generates a cryptographically random token,
  stores only its hash, expiry 15 minutes, single use. Returns the raw token
  (shown once as a code AND a QR payload). Limit active invitations per elder
  to 1 (creating a new one invalidates the old one).
- redeem-invitation: guardian submits the code. Rate-limit by user and IP
  (for example 5 attempts per 15 minutes) and increment the attempts counter;
  lock the invitation after 5 failed tries. Constant-time hash comparison. On
  success create a PENDING family_connection (not active) and an audit entry.
  Never reveal whether a code existed, was expired, or was used (one generic
  error).
- approve-connection: elder only. Moves pending -> active and sets share_level
  chosen by the elder. Records an audit entry.
- revoke-connection: elder or guardian. Immediate effect.
- update-share-level: elder only.
- get-entitlements: returns what the user's plan allows (see section 6).
- sync-incident: elder only, requires an active connection with a share level
  that allows it, and the user's explicit sync consent. Accepts only the
  Incident contract fields; rejects any extra field or any string field that
  looks like free text longer than the category limit. Creates incident and
  indicator rows.
