  query string and fragment, lowercase host, reject non-http(s), reject
  private/loopback/link-local IPs and internal hostnames).
- Do NOT fetch or follow redirects in this layer (no server-side URL
  fetching, so no SSRF surface). Shortened links are only flagged by local
  rules; note redirect expansion as a future, hardened feature.
- Prefer the privacy-preserving hash-prefix approach if the current Safe
  Browsing API version supports it; otherwise use the Lookup API. Check the
  current API terms (including any non-commercial restriction and quota) and
  record what you found in docs/SECURITY_NOTES.md. Provider is hidden behind a
  UrlReputationProvider interface with a mock for dev.
- Client: after the local scan, if cloud URL check is enabled and URLs exist,
  call check-url and, if a URL is flagged, apply the result through a NEW
  engine module packages/engine/src/externalSignals.ts:
