  zero-width stripping, Malayalam chillu/ZWJ/ZWNJ normalisation, homoglyph
  and digit mapping, spaced-letter collapsing, Malayalam/Devanagari digit
  handling, URL/domain extraction), rule evaluation with per-signal
  de-duplication, LEGIT_CONTEXT negative signal, additive score with cap,
  overrides that only raise, thresholds, bilingual templates, determinism.
- REGEX PORTABILITY: JavaScript and Java regex dialects differ (lookbehind,
  named groups, Unicode classes, flags, \b semantics on non-Latin text).
  Add a rule-pack linter script in packages/engine (TypeScript, new module)
  that fails if any regex uses a construct outside an agreed portable
  subset, document that subset, and run it in the engine tests. If a
  conformance mismatch is caused by dialect differences, FIX THE RULE (make
  it portable) and keep both implementations passing. Never add
  Kotlin-only special cases for individual rules.
- Same ReDoS safety: enforce a per-scan time budget and input length cap in
  Kotlin as well, with a defined safe result (not a crash) when exceeded.
- Load the rule pack from an asset copied at build time from
  packages/engine/rulepacks (a Gradle task copies it so there is only one
  source). Expose getVersion() so web and native can show the same pack
  version.
- JVM unit tests (JUnit):
  a) Conformance runner: reads tests/conformance/vectors.json and asserts
